@* The mark for a stored payload: a page with lines of text on it. Drawn where a row offers its own
   JSON and on the header of the pop-up that opens, so what was clicked and what arrived look like
   the same thing.

   Its own mark rather than one of the section ones. Braces would be the obvious drawing and are
   already spoken for — they are what a declaration is written in, and the way into a type
   everywhere in this application, including the button across from the heading on the very pages
   this mark appears on. Two things under one mark is worse than no mark at all.

   Built to the same box, stroke and linecap as <see cref="SectionMark"/>, so a row carrying this
   and a row carrying one of those are drawn at one weight. Hidden from screen readers: the link
   around it is named, and read out this would be the same thing twice. *@
<svg class="glyph" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
     fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
    @* A sheet with its corner turned, which is what says page rather than box. *@
    <path d="M11.6 2.8H6.2a1.6 1.6 0 0 0-1.6 1.6v11.2a1.6 1.6 0 0 0 1.6 1.6h7.6a1.6 1.6 0 0 0 1.6-1.6V6.4z"/>
    <path d="M11.6 2.8v3.6h3.8"/>
    @* Two lines of it, short of the edges: enough to read as writing rather than as a ruled form. *@
    <path d="M7.6 10.4h4.8M7.6 13.4h3"/>
</svg>
